duorex

Sources/duorex/DuoScene.swift and Sources/duorex/ScreenSurface.swift contain code adapted from
serve-sim (https://github.com/EvanBacon/serve-sim), which is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

Adapted parts: the lookup of Apple's Duo model inside Xcode, the fold rig, the screen material
slots, and the skinned screen sampling. duorex changed them to render to a window at display
rate, to keep the model's own materials, and to find touches by ray instead of by projection.

The iPhone Duo model belongs to Apple. duorex reads it from the installed Xcode and does not
copy or redistribute it.
